On a macOS host (MAP_JIT, write-protected while a vCPU thread executes
translated code) tb_check_watchpoint() invalidates the TB from a store
helper without making the JIT region writable: the store-exclusive of
qemu_spin_lock(&tb->jmp_lock) then fails forever and the vCPU thread spins
on the first watchpoint hit. tb_phys_invalidate__locked() already brackets
the same work with qemu_thread_jit_write()/qemu_thread_jit_execute().

--- a/accel/tcg/tb-maint.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/tb-maint.c
@@ -957,2 +957,3 @@
 {
+    qemu_thread_jit_write();
     if (page_addr == -1 && tb_page_addr0(tb) != -1) {
@@ -964,2 +965,3 @@
     }
+    qemu_thread_jit_execute();
 }
